---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Nurçin Ehlimanoğlu — a one-person game studio"
  description="A one-person studio making small, exact games. Glow Catch is the first."
  current="studio">

  <section>
    <h1>A one-person studio making <span class="hit">small, exact</span> games.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each one is built around a single rule you can learn in four seconds and
      keep failing at for an hour. No tutorials to sit through, no meters to
      wait on — the game is the rule, and the rule is the difficulty.
    </p>

    <div class="shelf" style="margin-top: clamp(40px, 7vw, 76px);">
      <a class="obj" href="/glow-catch">
        <div class="thumb live"></div>
        <div class="label"><b>Glow Catch</b><span>2026</span></div>
      </a>
      <div class="obj" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="thumb soon"></div>
        <div class="label"><span style="color:var(--muted)">Next</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">—</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="squig"></div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:56px; text-align:right;">
        <div class="label" style="justify-content:flex-end">
          <a href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com" style="color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a>
        </div>
        <div class="label" style="color:var(--muted); justify-content:flex-end; margin-top:4px">
          Replies in three working days
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="speckle" style="margin: 0 calc(var(--pad) * -1); padding-left: var(--pad); padding-right: var(--pad);">
    <p class="kicker">How the games are made</p>
    <h2>One rule, tested until it is fair.</h2>
    <div class="cols" style="margin-top: 30px;">
      <div class="card yellowish">
        <h3>The rule comes first</h3>
        <p>A game starts as one sentence. If the sentence needs a second sentence
           to make sense, it is not the game yet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card mintish">
        <h3>Difficulty is measured, not guessed</h3>
        <p>Every level in Glow Catch was run through a simulation before a person
           saw it, so a level that is impossible is a bug rather than a surprise.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card pinkish">
        <h3>Nothing is drawn twice</h3>
        <p>The boards, the glow, the sounds — all generated in code at runtime.
           The whole game ships with almost no image files.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="kicker">Contact</p>
    <h2>A person answers this address.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Bug reports, press, and publishing questions all go to the same place —
      there is only one of us. Support requests get a reply within three working
      days; the <a href="/support" style="color:var(--ink)">support page</a>
      answers the common ones immediately.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <a class="pill filled" href="mailto:nehlimanoglu@gmail.com"
         style="text-decoration:none">nehlimanoglu@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>

</Base>
